description:
Change under review. Task: `resolveAgent` must return a typed `UnknownAgent` error instead of throwing, as the project's error-handling rule (neverthrow `Result`) requires. Acceptance: an unknown name gives `err({ type: "UnknownAgent", name })`; the `run` command logs it and exits 1; tests cover a known and an unknown name.

Added files are shown in full. For changed files, only the changed region is shown; the rest of the file is unchanged and compiles.

`src/agents/resolve.ts` (changed, lines 1-22):
```ts
1 import { err, ok, type Result } from "neverthrow";
2 import type { AgentConfig } from "./config.js";
3
4 export type ResolveError = { type: "UnknownAgent"; name: string };
5
6 // Looks up an agent by it's name.
7 export function resolveAgent(
8   name: string,
9   agents: Map<string, AgentConfig>,
10 ): Result<AgentConfig, ResolveError> {
11   const a: AgentConfig | undefined = agents.get(name);
12   if (a === undefined) {
13     return err({ type: "UnknownAgent", name: name });
14   } else {
15     return ok(a);
16   }
17 }
```

`src/commands/run.ts` (changed, lines 30-36):
```ts
30   const resolved = resolveAgent(args.agent, agents);
31   if (resolved.isErr()) {
32     log.error({ name: resolved.error.name }, "unknown agent")
33     return 1;
34   }
35   const agent = resolved.value;
36   return startAgent(agent, args);
```

`src/agents/__tests__/resolve.test.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import { expect, test } from "bun:test";
2 import { resolveAgent } from "../resolve.js";
3
4 const loom = { name: "loom", models: ["claude-opus-5-5"] };
5
6 test("a known name resolves", () => {
7   expect(resolveAgent("loom", new Map([["loom", loom]]))._unsafeUnwrap()).toBe(loom);
8 });
9
10 test("an unknown name is an UnknownAgent error", () => {
11   expect(resolveAgent("nope", new Map())._unsafeUnwrapErr()).toEqual({ type: "UnknownAgent", name: "nope" });
12 });
```

`src/commands/__tests__/run.test.ts` (changed, lines 40-44):
```ts
40 test("an unknown agent exits 1", async () => {
41   const code = await runCommand({ agent: "nope" }, { agents: new Map() });
42   expect(code).toBe(1);
43 });
```

CI on this change: `bun test` 112 pass, 0 fail; `bun run typecheck` exits 0; `bun run lint` exits 0 with 3 warnings (no-else-return at `src/agents/resolve.ts:14`, semi at `src/commands/run.ts:32`, no-inferrable-types at `src/agents/resolve.ts:11`). The project treats lint warnings as non-blocking.
